THE DEFECT, AND IT IS THE LARGEST THING ON THIS BOARD. The spec has asked for a
sun 36 degrees above the horizon since it was written. Every run this rig has
ever done rendered one at 82.
  production/specs/vignette-pieces.json   sun elevation_deg 36 azimuth_deg 205
  VignetteSpec.h SunPitchDeg(36) = -36.0  VignetteSpec.h SunYawDeg(205) = 25.0
  the committed verdict, every shot line   sunPitchYawRead=-82.0/25.0
YAW AGREES TO THE DECIMAL AND PITCH IS OFF BY EXACTLY 46.0. 25.0 is no engine
default, so the ask reached the ACTOR and died between the actor and the
COMPONENT: SpawnDirectional handed its FRotator to SpawnActor as the actor
rotation and never set the light component's rotation, and a directional
light's direction IS the forward axis of that component's world transform,
which is also what the readback reads. A 4 m lamp post casts 4/tan(36) = 5.5 m
at the asked elevation and 4/tan(82) = 0.56 m at the rendered one, A FACTOR OF
TEN, which is queue 197 (nothing casts a contact shadow) explained rather than
described, and it is why a HUNDREDFOLD of sun intensity on run 38 blew
highlights by three orders of magnitude and moved the dark end by 1.06 nulls:
the light was very nearly straight down the whole time.

THE FIX IS ONE LINE AND IT DOES NOT DEPEND ON THE MECHANISM. C->SetWorldRotation
states the world rotation absolutely, so the asked value arrives whatever
relative rotation the component was carrying. NOTHING HERE SUBTRACTS 46 and
nothing assumes -46 is Unreal's shipped default, because nobody has confirmed
that it is.

AND THE REASON IT SURVIVED, which is what the new keys are for. CLAUDE.md rule
6: vignette-spec-test.cpp:404 tested the ARITHMETIC, :2058 tested the FORMAT
STRING, and nothing tested that the number reached the light. The same rig
already differenced asked against read for the camera (shotCamAskedPitchYaw
beside shotCamReadPitchYaw) and for 22 props (propCentreWorstMm against the
file's own coordinates). THE LIGHTS WERE THE ONE ACTOR POPULATION NOBODY EVER
DIFFERENCED.

WHAT THE VERDICT GAINS, ALL OF IT FORMATTED IN THE TESTED LAYER:
  lightAim*        one whole-run line: asked, read and SIGNED RESIDUAL on both
                   axes for all four directional lights, with
                   lightAimAgreeing=N/of=M and lightAimWorstResidualDeg naming
                   the light and axis it was worst on. lightAimStatus=AGREES is
                   THE ONLY PASSING WORD and the step exits non-zero on
