                   1.0 degree and the line says in its own value that this is
                   NOT a measured tolerance: it separates the 46.0 fault from a
                   float round trip of order 1e-4. If any run prints a residual
                   between 0.001 and 1.0, THAT is the series a real bound comes
                   off.
  shotSunIntensityAsked / shotSkyIntensityAsked / shotCellAgrees
                   per frame, and cellAgree=N/of=M once per run. Run 38 printed
                   five rungs that all read sky 1.000 and one control row that
                   read 0.350 and NEVER PRINTED THE CROSS, so the cell that
                   mattered had never been rendered and nothing said so.
  band.ground.p95OverP05
                   a ROBUST within-frame ratio, and its stat string says
                   ROBUST-NOT-INVARIANT because a tonemap is MONOTONE, NOT
                   LINEAR: under a monotone map a ratio moves and only ORDER
                   survives. Quotable across cells only if the null cell held.
  band.ground.darkerThanSkyMedianPct
                   the EXACTLY INVARIANT one: the share of ground-band pixels
                   strictly darker than the skyCentre band's MEDIAN PIXEL OF
                   THE SAME FRAME. Its Ties and Rails ship beside it always,
                   because ties and the two rails are where the curve stops
                   being strictly monotone and the invariance claim stops being
                   true. The stat string names bloom, vignette, grain and local
                   tonemapping as the exceptions, which the ruling requires.
  fogMaxOpacityRead
                   asked beside read, now that the cap is a field.

