The retired ladder rendered in INCREASING order, so a drift ordered by shot was
perfectly confounded with a response to the light. CoreTests and
vignette-spec-test both print this sequence and both assert that it rises
somewhere and falls somewhere.

THE NULL CELL IS THE FIRST THING READ, AND IT IS BLOCKING. grid_null_repeat is
a field-for-field duplicate of grid_sky100_sun003, the grid's reference cell,
and it is THE LAST SHOT IN THE RUN while its twin is the second grid shot: every
other shot, every condition change and every light probe stands between them.
Both test layers assert the duplicate field by field, so a typo cannot make the
pair differ by an input. IF THE PAIR'S DIFFERENCE AT shotMeanLuma,
band.ground.p05 AND band.ground.p50 IS NOT SMALLER THAN THE SMALLEST SKY STEP
IN THE GRID ON ALL THREE, THE GRID IS A NO-READ: no cell is quoted and the
resident escalates. Run 38 carried this same test as ladder_sun003, IT FAILED
at 0.1106 of mean luma and 0.1172 at band.ground.p05, and nobody read it.

